{"name":"Tanzanite Blue","hex":"#114a6b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tanzanite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trichroic violet-blue variety of the mineral zoisite mined in Tanzania, used as a gemstone. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tanzanite"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tanzanite","blocks":[{"text":"Tanzanite is the blue and violet variety of the mineral zoisite. The color is caused by small amounts of vanadium. Tanzanite belongs to the epidote mineral group. Tanzanite is only found in Simanjiro District of Manyara Region in Tanzania, in a very small mining area approximately 7 km (4.3 mi) long and 2 km (1.2 mi) wide near the Mererani Hills."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Zo%C3%AFsite_%28Tanzanite%29.jpg/330px-Zo%C3%AFsite_%28Tanzanite%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanzanite","wikidata":"Q429942"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Craft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg/500px-Craft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Craft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg/500px-Craft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Craft work on tanzanite","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACraft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Trichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg/500px-Trichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Trichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg/500px-Trichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Multicolored tanzanite crystal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATrichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Trichroic_Tanzanite_Gem_-_blue%2C_violet_%26_purple.jpg/500px-Trichroic_Tanzanite_Gem_-_blue%2C_violet_%26_purple.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Trichroic_Tanzanite_Gem_-_blue%2C_violet_%26_purple.jpg/500px-Trichroic_Tanzanite_Gem_-_blue%2C_violet